---
title: AGENTS migration governance flow
---

flowchart TD
  accTitle: AGENTS.md (Technical)
  accDescr {
    Each contribution starts in a fresh task branch inside a disposable clone or isolated worktree. It is then classified as manual documentation, merge-triggered documentation, or site-code work. Manual documentation receives human review. The merge workflow publishes only a complete validated bundle. Site-code or mixed work uses an approved pull request. After publication, cleanup removes the disposable checkout only when remote work is preserved and the checkout is clean; otherwise it reports the blocker.
  }
  request["Contribution request"] --> checkout["Create fresh task branch in disposable clone or isolated worktree"]
  checkout --> automated{"Trusted merged-PR workflow?"}
  automated -->|Yes| codex["Codex drafts complete bundle without GitHub write access"]
  codex --> boundary{"Only allowed documentation paths changed?"}
  boundary -->|No| incident["Block publication and report failure"]
  boundary -->|Yes| provenance["Record repository, PRs, merge SHA, run, and source hash"]
  provenance --> validate["Run exact wiki validation commands"]
  automated -->|No| classify{"Documentation only?"}
  classify -->|Yes| bundle["Update canonical source, Simple mirror, Technical mirror, and diagram"]
  bundle --> review["Human reviews current Simple content and diagram"]
  review --> approve["Record current approval"]
  approve --> validate
  validate --> direct["Commit and push directly to main"]
  classify -->|No or mixed| branch["Create site-code branch"]
  branch --> pr["Open normal ready pull request"]
  pr --> checks["Require passing checks and explicit merge approval"]
  checks --> publish["Merge and publish"]
  direct --> publish
  publish --> safe{"Remote work preserved and checkout clean?"}
  safe -->|Yes| cleanup["Remove disposable checkout and prune worktree metadata"]
  safe -->|No| blocker["Keep checkout and report exact cleanup blocker"]
